# Things that must never be committed.
#
# The first two are the important ones. settings.json is written on first run
# and logs/ is written by every turn and every card decision, so neither is in
# the repository - and if either ever appears in `git ls-files`, a test fails.
# A secret in a git commit is a secret forever, because git keeps the history.

settings.json
logs/

# Python's own leftovers.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Anything that holds a credential. These should not exist here at all, which
# is the point of listing them: a .env that appears one day will not be
# committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# Notes written by the write_note action, and the owner's own editor folders.
notes/
.vscode/
.idea/
